commit bc34b7ec57828eceab52e7400ea096aec68ab440

C03: «abre un navegador y busca X» navigates to the public search page; weather medium before the noun; definition questions; constraint ack keeps its first sentence (WEB1455)

WEB1453 measured two boundary defects: «¿Qué es un pronóstico del tiempo?» was read as a weather lookup (the definition guard only knew «significa/definición») and a web.search started; and the acknowledgement of «No investigues nada en internet.» was rejected twice because the model appended a second sentence of universal offer, so a clarification question was published. WEB1291 had documented the search engine's off-topic results for generic queries; two Navegación y búsqueda web shapes do not depend on that relevance: «Abre un navegador que tengas instalado y busca Windows 11 settings» (unread until now) and «busca el clima en internet» (whose query kept «en internet» when the medium preceded the noun).

baxy_mind effect_intent: _installed_browser_search_query reads «abre/abrí un navegador (que tengas instalado) y busca X» — resolved in the clause-group resolver as one browser.navigate (reviewed), with the person's literal query (quotation marks removed); _weather_lookup_query drops «en internet/google/la web» before or after the noun and a leading article («busca en internet el clima» → «clima»); a question «qué es un/una …» / «what is a …» is a definition, never a weather, news, today's-events or research lookup.
baxy_mind __main__: the installed-browser search navigates to the product's public search page (Bing) with the literal query, confirmed as a complete URL like the named-browser search.
baxy_mind llm: a constraint acknowledgement keeps its first sentence when the whole reply fails the one-sentence contract and the first sentence alone meets it.

Offline probes: the three registry literals and both variants of the browser-search shape resolve to one browser.navigate with the Bing URL; «busca en internet el clima» → query «clima»; the definition questions resolve to nothing; the two WEB1453 acknowledgement drafts pass on their first sentence. Mind only (BUILD1455). Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


